WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.339
(soft melodious music)

00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:11.003
- [Narrator] Three and a quarter
miles east of Key Biscayne

00:00:11.003 --> 00:00:13.190
near Miami, Florida, is an underwater

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:17.074
eternal resting place for ocean lovers.

00:00:17.074 --> 00:00:20.962
The Neptune Memorial Reef is
an artificial, man-made reef

00:00:20.962 --> 00:00:24.529
that houses the remains
of thousands of people.

00:00:24.529 --> 00:00:27.177
After cremation, ashes
are mixed with cement

00:00:27.177 --> 00:00:31.560
to form features that
become part of the reef.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.011
The reef's design was inspired

00:00:33.011 --> 00:00:35.406
by the underwater city Atlantis

00:00:35.406 --> 00:00:38.167
and includes lion statues, columns,

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.584
benches, canopies and podiums.

00:00:42.258 --> 00:00:44.955
It takes up half an acre and sits 40 feet

00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:47.266
under the surface of the water.

00:00:47.266 --> 00:00:49.466
The Neptune Memorial Reef
serves a dual purpose

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:52.352
as a home to many underwater creatures,

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:56.519
fulfilling its mission of
creating life after life.

